// -*- mode:c++ -*-

// Xspm extension -- scratchpad DMA instructions.
// Uses custom-0 opcode space (OPCODE5 = 0x02, full opcode = 0x0B).
//
// Instruction encoding:
//   spm.dma rd, rs1, rs2   R-type  funct3=0x0   Initiate async DMA
//   spm.dma.w              I-type  funct3=0x1   Wait for DMA completion

// spm.dma: R-type, reads Rs1 (DRAM source), Rs2 (byte count),
// Rd is both input (SPM destination address) and output (echoed back).
// Starts an async DMA transfer via the SpmDmaEngine.
def format SpmDmaOp(code, *opt_flags) {{
    iop = InstObjParams(name, Name, 'SpmDma', code,
        ['IsNonSpeculative'])
    header_output = BasicDeclare.subst(iop)
    decoder_output = BasicConstructor.subst(iop)
    decode_block = BasicDecode.subst(iop)
    exec_output = BasicExecute.subst(iop)
}};

// spm.dma.w: implemented as a Load from the DMA STATUS register.
// The SpmDmaEngine returns the current pending-transfer count
// immediately (polling semantics).  The compiler wraps this in a
// branch-back loop, e.g.:
//
//     spm.dma  rd, rs1, rs2    # enqueue transfer (non-speculative)
//   .poll:
//     spm.dma.w  rd            # rd ← pending count
//     bnez  rd, .poll          # spin until 0
//
// IsReadBarrier + IsWriteBarrier (memory barrier):
//   Ensures all prior memory operations (including the MMIO write
//   inside spm.dma) are visible before this load issues.  Unlike
//   IsNonSpeculative, the load enters the IQ normally and can issue
//   as soon as its memory-ordering constraints are met — it does NOT
//   have to wait at the ROB head.  This eliminates the commit-stage
//   stall that IsNonSpeculative caused on every DMA wait, enabling
//   better DMA/compute overlap in double-buffered kernels.
//
//   Ordering with the prior spm.dma is guaranteed because:
//     1) spm.dma is IsNonSpeculative → must commit before anything
//        after it in program order can reach the ROB head.
//     2) The barrier flags prevent the LSQ from issuing this load
//        until all prior loads/stores have drained.
//     3) In the unlikely event the load fires before spm.dma commits
//        (speculative execution), the DMA engine returns 0 (idle) and
//        the poll loop spins one extra iteration — the spm.dma will
//        commit in the meantime and the next poll sees the true status.
def format SpmDmaWaitOp(memacc_code,
        ea_code={{EA = 0xF0000018ULL;}},
        offset_code={{;}},
        mem_flags=[], inst_flags=[]) {{
    inst_flags += ['IsReadBarrier', 'IsWriteBarrier']
    (header_output, decoder_output, decode_block, exec_output) = \
        LoadStoreBase(name, Name, offset_code, ea_code, memacc_code,
        mem_flags, inst_flags, 'SpmDmaWait', exec_template_base='Load')
}};
